Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, with integration-test calibration applied (class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]` + project name `*.IntegrationTests`).

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4 of 8**     |

Half the tests are clean — `UpdateUser`, `DeleteUser`, `ListUsers`, and `ConcurrentInserts` are well-structured with clear AAA separation, specific assertions, and proper async usage.

---

## High-Severity Findings

### 1. Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. "Unknown Test") — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

The method inserts 100 users but never asserts anything. MSTest reports it as passing regardless of correctness.

```csharp
// BEFORE — exercises code, proves nothing
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### 2. Conditional Test Logic — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

The `if/else` means one branch is never exercised. The test asserts different things depending on the runtime type, hiding a gap.

```csharp
// BEFORE — one branch never runs
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two tests with deterministic setup, or assert the known type directly:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsStandardUser_WithCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

---

## Medium-Severity Findings

### 3. Sleepy Test — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

Uses `Thread.Sleep(3000)`, introducing a 3-second wall-clock wait. Even for integration tests this is a smell — it makes the suite slow and non-deterministic. Additionally, the method is `async Task` but uses a synchronous blocking sleep.

```csharp
// BEFORE
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry loop with a timeout, or `await Task.Delay` at minimum:

```csharp
// Preferred — poll with backoff
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
{
    if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
        break;
    await Task.Delay(100);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

---

### 4. Assertion Roulette — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

Contains **4 assertions with no message parameters**. When one fails, the MSTest output shows `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no context about *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add descriptive messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

---

## Smells Not Detected (15 of 19 — Clean)

| # | Smell | Status |
|---|-------|--------|
| 2 | Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean — uses in-memory SQLite, no external resources |
| 5 | Eager Test | ✅ Clean — multi-method calls are normal integration setup (calibrated) |
| 6 | Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean — all literals are contextually obvious (3 after 3 inserts, etc.) |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean — no `.ToString()` comparisons |
| 8 | Exception Handling | ✅ Clean — no `try`/`catch` in tests |
| 9 | General Fixture | ✅ Clean — `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| 10 | Ignored Test | ✅ Clean — no `[Ignore]` attributes |
| 11 | Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean — no repeated identical assertions |
| 12 | Lazy Test | ✅ Clean (calibrated — shared retrieval calls are normal for integration) |
| 13 | Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean — uses `[TestInitialize]` properly |
| 14 | Default Test | ✅ Clean — meaningful class name |
| 15 | Redundant Print | ✅ Clean — no debug output |
| 16 | Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean — no tautological assertions |
| 17 | Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean — hermetic in-memory database |
| 18 | Empty Test | ✅ Clean |

## Positive Observations

- **Proper lifecycle management** — `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` with `Dispose()` on the connection
- **Sealed test class** — follows MSTest v4 best practice
- **In-memory SQLite** — avoids real database dependency, hermetic and fast
- **Good naming convention** — `Method_Scenario` pattern is consistent across the suite
- **Proper async test** — `ConcurrentInserts` correctly uses `await Task.WhenAll`

## Prioritized Remediation

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test (`BulkInsert`) | Low — add 2 lines | Eliminates false confidence |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser`) | Medium — split into 2 tests | Removes hidden test gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert`) | Medium — add poll loop | Saves 3s per run, reduces flakiness |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser`) | Low — add message strings | Improves failure diagnosis |
